cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you refer to this software, please cite it using the metadata below. Cite
  it as a synthetic-only software demonstration. It reports no measurement and
  no scientific result, so it must not be cited as evidence for a rotation
  curve, a galactic-structure result, a calibration accuracy, an uncertainty,
  or a 21 cm detection.
title: galaxy-structure
abstract: >-
  A deterministic, synthetic-only demonstration of the software a 21 cm spectrum
  analysis needs: schema-validated ingestion with declared units, deterministic
  synthetic spectrum generation, deterministic interference injection and
  masking with an explicit record of every altered sample, frequency-to-velocity
  conversion under an explicit rest frequency and Doppler convention,
  byte-reproducible figures, and a run manifest. Every datum it handles is
  synthetic; it contains no measured observation. Real-observation calibration
  and reference-frame stages are present by name and fail closed, because the
  evidence they require was never established. The software was written for the
  rebuild of a physics final project by Dennis Wu and Alex Tong, who contributed
  equally to that project overall and collected its measurements together; those
  measurements are not included here. All code in this repository was written by
  Dennis Wu. Those attribution statements are the owner's, recorded as such and
  not independently verified.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wu
    given-names: Dennis
version: 0.1.0
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: https://github.com/denniswu28/phy417s
keywords:
  - synthetic data
  - reproducibility
  - spectrum analysis
  - radio astronomy software
  - unit safety
